{"explanation":"Add a dedicated EncryptedKey interface regression test while preserving both existing test methods and their assertions verbatim. The new test performs independent AES/GCM encrypted-key round trips for protected keys with different algorithms, indirectly verifying that each encrypted record retains the parameters and AAD metadata required by decrypt without asserting unstable ciphertext, nonce, or parameter bytes.","review_assumptions":["EncryptedKey does not expose retained AlgorithmParameters or ciphertext bytes publicly; successful decrypt round trips through its unchanged public interface are the available non-reflective verification that retained parameters can be decoded and that algorithm AAD remains usable.","Supported Android providers offer KeyGenerator support for AES and HmacSHA512 at 256 bits, as already required by the existing test."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"medium","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/EncryptedKeyTest.java","original_code":"    @Test
